## Model card (verified spec facts only)

- **Name:** Grok 5
- **Short description:** xAI's next flagship model — the fifth major iteration in the Grok series. Confirmed in training but NOT released as of 2026-09-29; every spec in circulation (6T–10T parameters, 1.5M context, AGI) is rumor or a Musk X post, not a published spec.
- **Provider / access:** None yet — no API endpoint, no model card, no `grok-5` entry in xAI's model docs as of writing. Expected to follow the Grok 4.7 pattern (xAI API, Cursor, Grok Build, third-party routers/clouds).
- **Release / knowledge:** Not released. xAI's January 2026 Series E funding announcement confirms the model exists and is in training (the only official reference). Release targets late-2025, Q1 2026, and Q2 2026 all passed with no launch; Musk's 2026-09-14 roadmap puts Grok 4.8 (2.5T, new C++ software stack) and Grok 4.9 ("probably Astra/Fable class") between the shipped Grok 4.7 (2026-09-21, current flagship, $2/$6 per 1M, 500K ctx) and Grok 5. Knowledge cutoff: n/a (unshipped).
- **IDs:** `grok-5` (expected; not yet listed in xAI docs — no Free ID)
- **Context window:** no verified public data found — the widely repeated ~1.5M tokens is an estimate; shipping Grok 4.7 is 500K, Grok 4.3 was 1M, Grok Build is 256K
- **Modalities:** no verified public data found — native multimodal and live X data are "expected" per Grok's direction but unspecified for Grok 5
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-02):** no verified public data found — xAI has not announced Grok 5 pricing; the current flagship Grok 4.7 is $2/$6 per 1M (doubled past 200K-token prompts)
- **Architecture:** Confirmed: in training on the Colossus 2 supercluster (xAI, now SpaceXAI after the February 2026 SpaceX acquisition). Rumored: 6T–10T mixture-of-experts parameters — reporting disagrees on which figure belongs to Grok 5 versus sibling models training alongside it; no model card confirms any number.

