## Self-exclusion note

Zero verified public benchmark numbers exist for Grok 5 as of 2026-10-02 because the model has not shipped: it is confirmed in training (xAI January 2026 funding announcement; Colossus 2) with no model card, no spec sheet, no API endpoint, and no leaderboard entry (geotoolbox.ai, updated 2026-09-29; Grokipedia; Polymarket prices a release by 2026-12-31 at roughly a coin flip, 40–55%, with 2026-11-30 at 23%). All circulating specs — 6T–10T MoE parameters, ~1.5M context, Musk's AGI claim ("That will be Grok 5", 2026-09-14, up from "10% and rising", October 2025), and the "Reality Engine" fact-checker — are Musk posts, leaks, or blog-coined labels, none published by xAI as a verified spec or benchmark. Spring 2026 headlines mislabeled the ~1.5T V9-Medium foundation (shipped as Grok 4.5/4.6) as "Grok 5" — a different model. Saved as `.md.excluded` per the mandatory self-exclusion rule (`RULES.md`, `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`): no scores computed, no placeholder numbers invented.

